{
  "content": {
    "body": "This is the BASE component catalog for a **model** pebble — one persisted\ndatabase table/model. It DEFINES every component (category) and WHAT\nbelongs under it. Other knowledge and skills — extraction, verification,\nfix — REFERENCE this doc to learn what goes under `name`, `type`,\n`reference key`, a relationship, etc.; they own the METHOD (how to capture\nor prove), this doc owns the DEFINITIONS they populate.\n\nRead each entry as: the component, then the values/shape considered part\nof it.\n\n## Pebble-level components\n\n- **name** — the model's identifier. Under it: one string equal to the\n  table/model name in the codebase.\n- **status** — the model's spec↔code alignment. Under it: ONE of the status\n  vocabulary — planned · in-progress · implemented · verified · drift ·\n  broken · missing · deprecated.\n- **description** — prose. Under it: what the model stores, why it exists,\n  its role in the domain.\n- **checklist reference** — a link to a checklist pebble. Under it: the\n  requirement / acceptance items that gate an implement / verify / fix of\n  this model. Present only when there is such an intent; otherwise the\n  model's own status carries the disposition.\n- **model references** — pebble→pebble edges to OTHER model pebbles. Under\n  it: every model this one connects to, from BOTH sources below (field\n  reference keys AND relationships), captured in both directions.\n- **findings references** — links to finding pebbles. Under it: dated,\n  append-only evidence for anything (a field, constraint, relationship or\n  checklist item) that does not meet spec.\n- **resources** — the model's ENTRY POINTS into the codebase (code links).\n  PURPOSE: a resource tells the AI the EXACT file — optionally a symbol and\n  line — to open FIRST when it needs to investigate, understand, verify or\n  fix this model, so it starts from the real code instead of re-discovering\n  where the model lives. Whenever the AI reads a source file that concerns\n  this model (its migration, model/entity class, schema), it SHOULD link it\n  here — the accumulated links make later discovery instant. To find the\n  file, use the code map (`map-search` / `map-file` / `map-symbol`); the\n  user does the same manually via the app's Mapping feature. Bind with\n  `link-code`, remove with `unlink-code` (the target file must exist).\n  Under it: a list of { path, symbol?, line?, note? }. Resources point at\n  CODE — NOT at other pebbles the way references do.\n\nRules are NOT a component of a model.\n\n## Field components — the categories under each field (column)\n\n- **name** — the column/attribute identifier. Under it: one string matching\n  the code.\n- **type** — the field's datatype. Under it, ONE of:\n  - a DB type from the vocabulary, grouped by category — character/text ·\n    numeric · boolean · date/time · binary · structured/special (the union\n    across MySQL / PostgreSQL / Oracle);\n  - a **Custom…** verbatim type (when the real type isn't in the list);\n  - a **nested typeRef** — the field's type IS another table/structure\n    pebble (the `type` then shows that pebble's display name).\n- **pk** (primary key) — a boolean marker. Under it: whether the field is\n  (part of) the primary key; composite keys mark every participating column.\n- **reference key** (FK) — a REFERENCE (kind 1). Under it: the target\n  **model** and the target **field** it points at — captured as\n  { model, field } and resolved to { pebbleId, path, fieldId, label } where\n  label reads \"Model.field\".\n- **nullable** — a boolean. Under it: whether NULL is allowed. Stored as\n  `required` (= NOT NULL) and shown INVERTED in the app as \"Nullable\".\n- **default** — the default value. Under it: the verbatim literal or\n  expression (`false`, `0`, `now()`, `[]`), or none.\n- **status** — the field's own spec↔code alignment. Under it: the SAME\n  status vocabulary as the pebble.\n- **description** — prose. Under it: the column's meaning, unit, allowed\n  values, gotchas.\n\n## Relationship components — the categories under each relationship\n\n- **name** — the relationship's accessor/method name. Under it: one string\n  matching the code's relation name (method / function / property).\n- **model** (target) — a REFERENCE (kind 2). Under it: the related **model**\n  pebble (ANY model), captured as { path } and resolved to a { pebbleId }\n  graph edge. May have NO local FK column — the FK can live on the other\n  side, or it joins on an arbitrary field / pivot.\n- **type** — the association kind. Under it: ONE of — has-one · has-many ·\n  belongs-to · belongs-to-many · has-one-through · has-many-through ·\n  morph-one · morph-many · morph-to.\n- **description** — prose (optional). Under it: a free note, typically the\n  join field, pivot, or through model.\n\n## References — the two kinds the graph captures\n\nA model connects to another model in exactly two ways, and BOTH become\npebble→pebble edges recorded in **model references** (visible both ways):\n\n1. **Field reference key (FK)** — a column whose value points at another\n   model's field. Lives on a field as `refKey`.\n2. **Relationship target** — a named association to another model, possibly\n   with NO local FK column. Lives on a relationship as `target`.\n\n## Quick map — category → what's under it\n\n| Component | Under it (shape / allowed values) |\n|---|---|\n| pebble.name | table/model name (string) |\n| pebble.status | planned·in-progress·implemented·verified·drift·broken·missing·deprecated |\n| pebble.description | prose: what / why / purpose |\n| checklist reference | link → checklist pebble (requirement items) |\n| model references | edges → other model pebbles (from FKs + relationships) |\n| findings references | links → finding pebbles |\n| resources | code links → { path, symbol?, line?, note? } to the implementing files |\n| field.name | column name (string) |\n| field.type | DB type (character/numeric/boolean/date-time/binary/structured) · Custom… · nested typeRef |\n| field.pk | boolean (part of primary key) |\n| field.reference key | { model, field } → resolved refKey (\"Model.field\") |\n| field.nullable | boolean (stored as required = NOT NULL) |\n| field.default | verbatim literal / expression, or none |\n| field.status | same status vocabulary |\n| field.description | prose |\n| relationship.name | accessor / method name (string) |\n| relationship.model | { model } → resolved graph edge (any model) |\n| relationship.type | has-one·has-many·belongs-to·belongs-to-many·*-through·morph-* |\n| relationship.description | prose (join / pivot note) |\n\n## Model CLI — all model pebble operations live here\n\nEvery model mutation goes through `pebbles-cli` (never hand-edit `.pebble`\nfiles). `content` is sent WHOLE. The write is HARDENED for the components\nabove:\n\n- every field must carry a **name, type, description and status** —\n  incomplete fields are rejected, listing exactly what's missing;\n- a **reference key** and a **relationship target** are auto-captured: the\n  CLI resolves the target model's real `pebbleId` (a field NAME is accepted\n  in place of a fieldId) and mirrors the edge at the pebble level, so BOTH\n  models show the connection in `refs`;\n- a link whose target does not exist is DROPPED and reported in\n  `droppedRefs` — create the target first;\n- there is NO delete: retire a model with status `deprecated`.\n\nCREATE — a model with fields (PK + FK) and relationships (incl. one with no\nlocal FK column):\n\n    pebbles-cli create models --title \"Service Request\" --content '{\n      \"kind\": \"fields\",\n      \"fields\": [\n        { \"name\": \"id\", \"type\": \"bigint unsigned\", \"required\": true,\n          \"primaryKey\": true, \"status\": \"implemented\",\n          \"description\": \"Surrogate primary key\" },\n        { \"name\": \"customer_id\", \"type\": \"bigint unsigned\", \"required\": true,\n          \"status\": \"implemented\", \"description\": \"Owning customer\",\n          \"refKey\": { \"path\": \"models/customer.pebble\", \"field\": \"id\" } },\n        { \"name\": \"status\", \"type\": \"enum\", \"required\": true,\n          \"default\": \"open\", \"status\": \"implemented\",\n          \"description\": \"Lifecycle state: open|assigned|closed\" }\n      ],\n      \"relationships\": [\n        { \"name\": \"customer\", \"type\": \"belongs-to\",\n          \"target\": { \"path\": \"models/customer.pebble\" },\n          \"description\": \"FK customer_id -> customers.id\" },\n        { \"name\": \"assignees\", \"type\": \"belongs-to-many\",\n          \"target\": { \"path\": \"models/user.pebble\" },\n          \"description\": \"via service_request_user pivot (no local FK)\" }\n      ]\n    }'\n\nUPDATE — top-level keys merge; `content` is replaced WHOLE (send the full\nfields + relationships). Units match by id, or by name when a unit has no\nid, inheriting prior id / status / description when omitted:\n\n    pebbles-cli update models/service-request.pebble --patch '{ \"description\": \"A work order raised by a customer\", \"content\": { \"kind\": \"fields\", \"fields\": [ ...full list... ], \"relationships\": [ ... ] } }'\n\nSTATUS — per field or whole model:\n\n    pebbles-cli set-status models/service-request.pebble verified --unit <fieldId>\n    pebbles-cli set-status models/service-request.pebble drift\n\nFINDING — attach evidence when a component doesn't meet spec:\n\n    pebbles-cli add-finding models/service-request.pebble --title \"customer_id missing FK constraint\" --category spec-violation --body \"Migration adds customer_id but declares no FK constraint (database/migrations/..._create_service_requests L18)\"\n\nINSPECT — connections BOTH ways (FK + relationship edges + backlinks),\nread, validate:\n\n    pebbles-cli refs models/service-request.pebble\n    pebbles-cli get models/service-request.pebble\n    pebbles-cli validate models/service-request.pebble\n\nRESOURCES — link the implementing code (the file must exist in the project):\n\n    pebbles-cli link-code models/service-request.pebble --file app/Models/ServiceRequest.php --symbol ServiceRequest\n    pebbles-cli unlink-code models/service-request.pebble --id <linkId>\n\nDEPRECATE (the \"delete\"):\n\n    pebbles-cli set-status models/service-request.pebble deprecated\n\n## Method lives elsewhere\n\nThis doc DEFINES the components. HOW to fill them from a codebase\n(extraction) or prove them against it (verification) lives in the\n**extraction-by-kind** and **verification-model** docs, which reference the\ncategories above.",
    "kind": "text"
  },
  "createdAt": "2026-07-27T14:50:52.082Z",
  "description": "The component CATALOG of a Model pebble: every part and WHAT belongs under it — pebble level (name, status, description, checklist / model / findings references), each field's categories (name, type, PK, reference key, nullable, default, status, description), each relationship's categories (name, target model, type), the two kinds of reference the graph captures, and every model-related pebbles-cli command. A DEFINITION reference other skills point at to learn what goes under each category — it describes the pieces, it doesn't prescribe method.",
